WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.629
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:15.971
Unit ten: Making Decisions. In this unit, you will compare choices and ask for advice.

4
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:17.915
Decision.

5
00:00:18.615 --> 00:00:21.404
Decision means a choice you make after thinking.

6
00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:24.005
Choosing a school is a big decision.

7
00:00:24.705 --> 00:00:27.311
Your turn. Say: Decision.

8
00:00:30.011 --> 00:00:30.908
Decision.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:32.720
Choice.

10
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.606
Choice means one thing you choose from many.

11
00:00:35.906 --> 00:00:38.834
You have two choices: tea or juice.

12
00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.012
Your turn. Say: Choice.

13
00:00:44.712 --> 00:00:45.678
Choice.

14
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.475
Option.

15
00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:50.384
Option means something you can choose.

16
00:00:50.684 --> 00:00:52.892
Another option is to take the bus.

17
00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:56.094
Your turn. Say: Option.

18
00:00:58.794 --> 00:00:59.551
Option.

19
00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:01.563
Advantage.

20
00:01:02.263 --> 00:01:04.494
Advantage means a good point about something.

21
00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:07.189
An advantage of cycling is that it's healthy.

22
00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:10.936
Your turn. Say: Advantage.

23
00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:14.637
Advantage.

24
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.744
Disadvantage.

25
00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.896
Disadvantage means a bad point about something.

26
00:01:20.196 --> 00:01:22.138
A disadvantage is that it's slow.

27
00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:25.606
Your turn. Say: Disadvantage.

28
00:01:28.306 --> 00:01:29.528
Disadvantage.

29
00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:31.169
Think.

30
00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:34.101
Think means to consider something carefully.

31
00:01:34.401 --> 00:01:35.832
Think before you decide.

32
00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:38.975
Your turn. Say: Think.

33
00:01:41.675 --> 00:01:42.456
Think.

34
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.463
Advice.

35
00:01:45.163 --> 00:01:48.149
Advice means an idea from someone about what you should do.

36
00:01:48.449 --> 00:01:50.414
My dad gave me good advice.

37
00:01:51.114 --> 00:01:53.905
Your turn. Say: Advice.

38
00:01:56.605 --> 00:01:57.583
Advice.

39
00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.619
Decide.

40
00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.655
Decide means to choose after thinking.

41
00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.060
I decided to join the art club.

42
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.992
Your turn. Say: Decide.

43
00:02:11.692 --> 00:02:12.496
Decide.

44
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.494
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:18.644
Sreypich, you look busy. What's up?

46
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.484
Should I join the art club or the football club?

47
00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:25.969
What are the advantages of each option?

48
00:02:27.283 --> 00:02:30.873
Art is relaxing, but football is good exercise.

49
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:34.729
My advice is to think about what you love most.

50
00:02:36.017 --> 00:02:39.821
I love drawing. I've decided! I'll join the art club.

51
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:43.418
Grammar focus: Should I or?.

52
00:02:43.718 --> 00:02:45.509
Should I take the bus or walk?

53
00:02:45.809 --> 00:02:49.178
Use 'Should I...?' to ask for advice when you have two options.

54
00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:53.103
Now read and listen. A Difficult Choice.

55
00:02:53.403 --> 00:02:56.296
Last week, I had a big decision to make.

56
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:00.163
Should I spend my money on a new bag or save it?

57
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.937
A new bag has an advantage: it looks great.

58
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.178
But saving money has a bigger advantage for my future.

59
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:12.841
I asked my mum for advice, and I decided to save.

60
00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.756
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:17.056 --> 00:03:19.044
blank I walk or take the bus?

62
00:03:19.344 --> 00:03:22.243
A, Should. B, Do. C, Am.

63
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.273
The answer is A: Should.

64
00:03:29.783 --> 00:03:31.945
A good point about something is an blank.

65
00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:36.143
A, advantage. B, disadvantage. C, option.

66
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.312
The answer is A: advantage.

67
00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:46.432
An idea from someone about what you should do is blank.

68
00:03:46.732 --> 00:03:50.466
A, advice. B, choice. C, decision.

69
00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.670
The answer is A: advice.

70
00:03:58.183 --> 00:04:01.358
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you make a big decision?

71
00:04:06.658 --> 00:04:13.084
First, I think about the advantages and disadvantages. Then I ask my parents for advice before I decide.

72
00:04:13.384 --> 00:04:15.465
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.089
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should i or?.

74
00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:25.038
Today's value is wisdom. Think carefully and listen to good advice before you decide.

75
00:04:25.338 --> 00:04:27.619
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:30.931
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

